# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, normalization depends on each contributor's local
# `core.autocrlf`, which is a machine setting and not a property of the
# repository. On this machine autocrlf=true happens to store LF correctly, but
# a contributor with autocrlf=false on Windows would commit CRLF into the
# blobs, and nothing in the repo would have said otherwise. Make it explicit.
#
# What matters is what git STORES, not what sits in the working tree — the
# stored blob is what a hash or byte comparison reads. Working-tree files may
# still appear CRLF on Windows; that is checkout behaviour and is fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# LICENSE is byte-compared and hashed by license scanners and by anyone
# verifying a fork carries an unmodified notice. A single differing byte —
# including a line ending — makes it read as non-canonical. Pinned explicitly
# rather than relying on the wildcard above.
LICENSE* text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they fail to execute on POSIX.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary
